{"id": "EUVD-2026-59700", "enisaUuid": "f7d11b27-129a-326d-9485-1f7e5d21b049", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: HIDP: validate numbered report payloads\n\nWhen hidp_get_raw_report() waits for a numbered report,\nhidp_process_data() compares the expected report number with skb->data[0].\nA connected HIDP peer can reply with only a DATA transaction header,\nleaving the skb empty after the header is removed.\n\nKMSAN reports an uninitialized-value use in hidp_session_run(), with the\nvalue originating in __alloc_skb() through vhci_write(). The transaction\nheader checks remove the empty-frame reports, but this report remains until\nthe payload check is added.\n\nThe comparison can also consume a peer-controlled byte beyond the declared\nL2CAP PDU. A DATA | FEATURE response followed by an extra 0x01 byte made\nthe current code accept that byte as report ID 1 and complete\nHIDIOCGFEATURE with a zero-byte result. With this change the malformed\nresponse is rejected with -EIO, while a subsequent valid response still\nsucceeds.\n\nRequire a payload byte before comparing a numbered report ID. Unnumbered\nreports continue to accept an empty payload.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T12:27:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:05:51", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:N", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/011bf4350d941f1995b2bd4b815ee206cacf2b8e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/689d8bb7fee96b7196b572b015b6055c6616ce0c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c73beb320f5705e508bf7d385b8cc5ef8d9c8b69", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b7ad105d46acd828e424454815e4cd31069e047a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7e7162427659b70ea17cd41b1f79e2e64c246690", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/27cc0e603355c585f1e5da8398faa4d36d498188", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9c841f59e10b5d75c398a3fc6b2da448d2a2276b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/34f53d27b81a16a02828c8fdfa4e02badc326f17"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74507", "GHSA-m9hx-hxv2-v7fm"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "000d8bde-71fb-3b47-a1a7-273f03fa770c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0ff1731a1ae51e8e48cd559d70db536281c47f8e <34f53d27b81a16a02828c8fdfa4e02badc326f17"}, {"id": "044d29cc-afda-3cc0-9fa5-439b556f3186", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.151"}, {"id": "24bee582-86e6-3867-91d6-21e333c41e1f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.44"}, {"id": "28fb132c-313a-323e-a374-a50d5d26d4f6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.216"}, {"id": "2cc4494f-e2cd-3942-99f9-d3a98d333a8e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0ff1731a1ae51e8e48cd559d70db536281c47f8e <9c841f59e10b5d75c398a3fc6b2da448d2a2276b"}, {"id": "3718e8e4-acc0-3571-bf59-595c998f0185", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.39"}, {"id": "5b46f56a-3fdc-3ad1-8096-35e1a03d9018", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0ff1731a1ae51e8e48cd559d70db536281c47f8e <7e7162427659b70ea17cd41b1f79e2e64c246690"}, {"id": "6e3e0fda-0f97-3ff3-ba61-5f0bad1cee17", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.103"}, {"id": "7463525c-c38c-3661-a841-4149261b1f56", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.8"}, {"id": "78f6a759-08ae-327b-bb28-4c6203533108", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.265"}, {"id": "84663ff1-39ee-3010-967f-d1f84de8faf6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0ff1731a1ae51e8e48cd559d70db536281c47f8e <011bf4350d941f1995b2bd4b815ee206cacf2b8e"}, {"id